! vfl_cross_tomemory.strap -- the three VFL model limits of docs/NEXT.md
! "EVERY OP THE MODEL STILL SETS" group B, built 2026-11-17:
!
!   1. M+, M+1, M+MG with a field that crosses a word boundary (blocks X);
!   2. a to-memory field whose SECOND word is below 32 -- ST, M+1, CM
!      into the index registers (blocks T);
!   3. a crossing field that also needs a progressive refill: three reads
!      (blocks R).
!
! Each was refused with OP; none is a documented restriction.
!
! WHAT THE MACHINE DOES, FROM THE PAGES (Reference Manual 22-6530-2, PDF =
! printed + 3, read in the page images):
!
!   printed p.55: a VFL data field "may start at any bit position in
!   storage".  printed p.56, Field Definition: "The storage word or word
!   pair which contains the addressed memory field is brought from storage
!   to the arithmetic section of the computer ... In integer arithmetic
!   operations that affect storage, such as STORE and ADD TO MEMORY, the
!   result replaces the storage operand in the bit positions specified by
!   the address and field length.  Data to the right or left of the
!   specified field in storage are never affected."
!
!   printed p.34, Special Registers: "Except as noted in connection with
!   the individual registers, addresses 1-15 are valid word addresses in
!   all but the following cases" -- seven cases (instructions, refill
!   addresses, I/O control words, I/O data, the instruction counter, EXIC's
!   pseudo-counter, RENAME), none a data store.  The index registers
!   (16-31) are not in that list at all.
!
!   printed p.21: "For code 3, addition and counting take place and also
!   the index specified by I is refilled if the count reaches zero";
!   printed p.21-22, Programming Notes: "An operation in which progressive
!   indexing is specified is executed in two parts.  The variable field
!   length part of the operation is prepared and then the index
!   modification portion of the operation is performed"; "If the index
!   register specified by the I field of an operation using progressive
!   indexing is an operand in the variable field length portion of the
!   operation, the original value of this index register will be used."
!
! So: a crossing field is the same operation with its bits in two words;
! a second word below 32 is stored as any store to that register is; a
! crossing field with a refill reads both words, does the VFL part, then
! the index part with its refill.  Block T4 is the last sentence's case:
! the store's second word IS the progressive index register, the VFL part
! writes it, and the index part then replaces it with the ORIGINAL value
! advanced -- which is what an ordering that wrote the index first would
! get wrong.
!
! HOW THE EXPECTATIONS WERE DERIVED.  By hand, BEFORE the arms were built,
! from the field arithmetic: a field at bit address A of length L in the
! pair (W, W+1) is IBM bits A..A+L-1 of the 128-bit pair.  The arithmetic
! and indicators of each X case are those of the ONE-WORD case of the same
! name in decks/vfl_binary_memadd_indicators.strap (M1 ... M11, hand-
! derived there from printed pp.59, 62-63 and Figure 13): a crossing
! changes where the bits are, nothing else, so the indicator word must be
! the same number.  Every target word is filled with A5/5A outside the
! field, so a store that wrote a whole word, or the wrong half, shows.
!
!   X1  M+(BU,8,8)  acc 1, field FF at W+.60 (W low nibble F, W+1 top
!       nibble F): 256, the carry leaves the field: 00.  LC MOP RZ
!       0x20000000140 (= M1).
!   X2  M+(BU,8,8)  acc 1, field FE: FF.  MOP RGZ 0x120 (= M2).  CONTROL.
!   X3  M+(BU,8,8)  acc -5, field 03: 3 + -5 = -2, unsigned, magnitude
!       stored: 02.  LC MOP RLZ RN 0x20000000190 (= M3).
!   X4  M+MG(BU,8,8) acc -1, field FF: 00.  LC MOP RZ (= M4).
!   X5  M+1(BU,8) acc (16)102 (PF "not affected", p.63), field FF: 00.
!       LC MOP RZ (= M7).
!   X6  M-1(BU,8)  field 00: -1, unsigned, magnitude stored: 01.  LC MOP
!       RLZ RN (= M8).
!   X7  M+(B,16,8) at W+.56: acc +5, field -3 (numeric 03 in W's low
!       byte, sign byte 08 in W+1's top byte): +2, sign byte 00.  MOP RGZ
!       0x120 (= M9).
!   X8  M+(DU,8,4) decimal: acc 27, field 15 at W+.60: 42.  MOP RGZ
!       0x120 (printed p.61's decimal ADD TO MEMORY; no carry, no digit of
!       the accumulator above the field).
!
!   T1  ST(BU,32,8), $X3+.48 (word 19 bit 48): acc (16)12345678.  X3
!       bits 48-63 := 1234, X4 bits 0-15 := 5678.  Read back by SX.
!   T2  M+1(BU,8), $X5+.60: X5 low nibble F, X6 top nibble F: 00, LC MOP
!       RZ 0x20000000140.
!   T3  CM0101(BU,16,8), $X8+.56: acc (16)BEEF (connective 0101 stores
!       the accumulator field, MCP's SF).  X8 low byte := BE, X9 top byte
!       := EF.
!   T4  ST(V+I)(BU,16,8), .16($X7) with X7 = 22.56 (X6's bit 56), count 5:
!       X6 low byte := BE; word 23 (X7 itself) top byte := EF, and then the
!       index part puts X7's ORIGINAL word back advanced by the address
!       part, 16 bits (printed p.21: "the address part ... is added to the
!       value field"):
!       value 22.56 + 16 bits = 23.08 = bit 1480 = (16)5C8, count 5,
!       refill 1500: X7 = (16)0005C800001405DC.
!
!   R1  M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) at W+.60 with count 1: X1's arithmetic and the
!       refill.  LC MOP RZ, and the index result indicators from the
!       pre-refill state (p.21: count zero XCZ, value > 0 XVGZ):
!       0x20000009140 (= M11).  X7 := RFW, (16)01348000013405DC.
!   R2  ST(V+ICR)(BU,16,8) at T+.56, count 1: acc (16)BEEF.  T low byte
!       := BE, T+1 top byte := EF.  MOP RGZ XCZ XVGZ 0x9120.  X7 := RFW.
!   R3  CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,16,8) at T+.56, count 1: as R2.  The connective
!       indicators (MOP, RGZ for a non-zero result) and XCZ XVGZ: 0x9120.
!
! The read-arm case (a crossing + with a refill) is
! decks/vfl_progressive_refill_once.strap's P10, flipped from "refused"
! to "done once" in the same change.
!
! MEASURED INJECTIONS, 2026-11-17, observed failures (each in a scratch
! copy of the tree, never in the worktree; this deck's line and
! vfl_progressive_refill_once's):
!   I1 rl_tail_write drops its write (the special tail never lands):
!      FAILS T1_X4, T2_X6, T3_X9 -- the three tails into an index
!      register -- and nothing else.  T4's tail is X7 itself, which the
!      index part overwrites anyway.
!   I2 the index part's write before the tail (armIdx no longer waits
!      for pendingTailWrite; armTail waits for pendingIdxWrite instead):
!      FAILS T4_X7_index_part_last ONLY, = (16)EF05B800001405DC: the
!      tail's EF over the advanced index.  p.22's order is pinned by
!      this one check.
!   I3 the M+ arm's crossing tail not written: FAILS X1_W1 .. X8_W1 (all
!      eight), T2_X6 and R1_W1 -- every M+ crossing's second word -- and
!      no indicator check.
!   I4 a crossing ST with a refill taking the index from prefetch[1]
!      (the field's second word) instead of prefetch[2]: FAILS R2_X7
!      ONLY, = (16)5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A, the field word.
!   I5 the read arms' refill slot truncated to one bit (the old two-word
!      prefetch's index): this deck all green; FAILS R10_refilled = (16)AB
!      in vfl_progressive_refill_once, nothing else.
! X2 is the CONTROL: the one case with no Lost Carry (MOP RGZ, 0x120) --
! it passes on every injection that leaves the crossing's second word
! alone, and its X2_W1 fails with the others under I3.
! The first run of the finished model failed T4 alone, (16)0005B8...: the
! derivation was wrong, not the model.  Progressive indexing adds the
! instruction's address part (p.21), and the draft's 0($X7) adds nothing;
! the deck now has .16($X7).
        SLC, 1000.0
START   L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W1+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W2+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        L(B,16,8), N5
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W3+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        L(B,16,8), N1
        Z, $IND
        M+MG(BU,8,8), W4+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        L(BU,16,8), H0102
        Z, $IND
        M+1(BU,8), W5+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I5
        Z, $IND
        M-1(BU,8), W6+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I6
        L(BU,8,8), FIVE
        Z, $IND
        M+(B,16,8), W7+.56
        TI, 1, $IND, I7
        L(DU,8,4), D27
        Z, $IND
        M+(DU,8,4), W8+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I8
! ---- T: the second word below 32 ----------------------------------
        LX, $X3, IX3
        LX, $X4, IX4
        L(BU,32,8), D32
        ST(BU,32,8), $X3+.48
        SX, $X3, S3
        SX, $X4, S4
        LX, $X5, IX5
        LX, $X6, IX6
        Z, $IND
        M+1(BU,8), $X5+.60
        TI, 1, $IND, I9
        SX, $X5, S5
        SX, $X6, S6
        LX, $X8, IX8
        LX, $X9, IX9
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        CM0101(BU,16,8), $X8+.56
        SX, $X8, S8
        SX, $X9, S9
        LX, $X6, IX6B
        LX, $X7, XPT
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        ST(V+I)(BU,16,8), .16($X7)
        SX, $X6, S6B
        SX, $X7, S7
! ---- R: a crossing field and a refill ---------------------------
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        LX, $X7, XPM
        Z, $IND
        M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X7), 0
        TI, 1, $IND, I10
        SX, $X7, R1
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        LX, $X7, XPS
        Z, $IND
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,16,8), 0($X7), 0
        TI, 1, $IND, I11
        SX, $X7, R2
        L(BU,16,8), HBEEF
        LX, $X7, XPC
        Z, $IND
        CM0101(V+ICR)(BU,16,8), 0($X7), 0
        TI, 1, $IND, I12
        SX, $X7, R3
        BOP, $                       ! hang if anything was refused
PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, 1500.0
XPM     XW, W11+.60, 1, RFW      ! count 1: the refill fires
XPS     XW, T1+.56, 1, RFW
XPC     XW, T2+.56, 1, RFW
XPT     XW, 22.56, 5, 1500.0     ! X6's bit 56; V+I does not count
RFW     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0   ! the refilled index word
N5      DD(BU,64), (16)0508000000000000
N1      DD(BU,64), (16)0108000000000000
ONE     DD(BU,64), (16)0100000000000000
FIVE    DD(BU,64), (16)0500000000000000
H0102   DD(BU,64), (16)0102000000000000
HBEEF   DD(BU,64), (16)BEEF000000000000
D27     DD(BU,64), (16)2700000000000000
D32     DD(BU,64), (16)1234567800000000
IX3     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A505A5A5A5A5
IX4     DD(BU,64), (16)5A5A5A0A5A5A5A5A
IX5     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A505A5A5A5AF
IX6     DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A505A5A5A5A5
IX8     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A505A5A5A5A5
IX9     DD(BU,64), (16)5A5A5A0A5A5A5A5A
IX6B    DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A505A5A5A5A5

        SLC, 1600.0
W1      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W2      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)E5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W3      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A0
        DD(BU,64), (16)35A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W4      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W5      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W6      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A0
        DD(BU,64), (16)05A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W7      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A503
        DD(BU,64), (16)08A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W8      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A1
        DD(BU,64), (16)55A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
W11     DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5AF
        DD(BU,64), (16)F5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
T1      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
        DD(BU,64), (16)5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A
T2      DD(BU,64), (16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
        DD(BU,64), (16)5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A

        SLC, 1700.0
I1      DD(BU,64), 0
I2      DD(BU,64), 0
I3      DD(BU,64), 0
I4      DD(BU,64), 0
I5      DD(BU,64), 0
I6      DD(BU,64), 0
I7      DD(BU,64), 0
I8      DD(BU,64), 0
I9      DD(BU,64), 0
I10     DD(BU,64), 0
I11     DD(BU,64), 0
I12     DD(BU,64), 0
S3      DD(BU,64), 0
S4      DD(BU,64), 0
S5      DD(BU,64), 0
S6      DD(BU,64), 0
S8      DD(BU,64), 0
S9      DD(BU,64), 0
S6B     DD(BU,64), 0
S7      DD(BU,64), 0
R1      DD(BU,64), 0
R2      DD(BU,64), 0
R3      DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
